{:event/actor "seb" :event/at #inst "2026-07-29T17:41:19.375Z" :event/body {:fact/path [:summary] :fact/value "f(events, now) is literally true but invites reading the reached set as a function of the state. It is a function of the whole trajectory via sticky-ever (stage.cljc:71), so a late-arriving backdated event can REMOVE a sticky reach a replica previously derived. Once reached always reached holds within one fold, not across the union of two event sets - and ADR 0019 has effects observing frontier transitions, so a reach can fire an unringable bell that a later sync retracts. Say plainly in the docstrings and the plan that sticky is monotone in fold position, not in the event set."} :event/parents #{"sha256-d9ed9ae56bbe238f9c7feb6d595e7526590abeadd9a08a8eded76f6ae62d8171"} :event/ticket #uuid "55c46156-2db2-42f4-9429-4845fd640940" :event/type :fact/assert}